t 1240. Actually original SHOP.CO kit: container 1240, margins 100. I'll go: frame 1440, padding 100 → content 1240.\n\nWait, but product cards: 4 per row in home: 4×295 + 3×16 = 1180+48... Let me compute: content 1240, gap 20, 4 cards: (1240-60)/4 = 295 each. Good.\n\nCategory: filters 296 + gap 64? Filters sidebar ~296, products 9 grid 3 cols. \n\nProduct page: gallery 444 + info 656.\n\nCart: items 715 + summary 400.\n\n**Component list to build in workspace (as components):**\n1. Button variants: Primary (default black), White (white bg black text), Outline? Brief says default Button given — I can copy instance and override. I'll create Button/Primary and Button/White components.\n2. Text Field — default given; I'll create search field variant, newsletter field, promo field as instances with overrides.\n3. AnnouncementBar\n4. Header (default + with current Shop)\n5. Footer\n6. ProductCard (default: image, name, rating, price, old price, discount) — variants with/without discount handled via visibility or overrides\n7. StyleTile (dress style card)\n8. ReviewCard (home)\n9. ProductReviewCard (product page)\n10. Newsletter\n11. SectionHeading (title + arrow buttons)\n12. RatingStars component\n13. Pagination\n14. QuantityStepper\n15. ColorSwatch\n16. SizeChip\n17. FilterSection etc.\n\nGiven the huge amount of work, components + 4 full frames, I need to be efficient. The benchmark evaluates: checklist coverage, data accuracy, flow/prototype, hierarchy, visual quality, component reuse, state design.\n\nStrategy: Build components on the workspace page first (in a \"Components\" area off to the side), then assemble frames using instances.\n\nActually, since brief says \"Design all other states, the header, the footer, the navigation and every business component as reusable components in your file\" — I should create components. To be efficient, I'll create components for: Announcement Bar, Header (2 states could be one component with text color override), Footer, ProductCard, StyleTile, ReviewCard, Newsletter, SectionHeader, RatingStars, Stepper, ColorSwatch, SizeChip, Pagination, ProductReviewCard. \n\nLet me think about how instances + overrides work: I can create a component, then use comp.createInstance(), place it, then modify text via setProperties or directly finding text children. Since component children are editable on instances (override), I can set .characters on instance text nodes directly. That works in the plugin API.\n\nHowever, one complication: icons from Media page are components? They're SYMBOL type in metadata. Let me check — in the metadata, they show as `<symbol>`. SYMBOL = COMPONENT node type in XML. So 4:5 Icon_Account etc. are COMPONENTS! And 4:36 Photo_Hero is a COMPONENT. And 1:23 Button, 1:26 Text Field are COMPONENTS. \n\nSo I can create instances of these directly. \"Copy these components into your own file and use them as instances\" — hmm, it says copy these components into your own file. But we're working in the same file, so I can just instance them directly from 04 · Media page. The instruction in the file says \"Copy these components into your own file and use them as instances\" — since the whole benchmark copy is our file, instancing directly from the Media page should be fine (Figma instances can live anywhere referencing components in the same file). That preserves reference pages while using instances in the workspace.\n\nImportant: DON'T move the originals. Just create instances in the workspace.\n\nPhotos are components with a fixed size (e.g., Photo_Hero component 147x220 inside a frame). Instances can be resized; images likely use scale mode FILL or FIT. Product photos are \"cut-outs on a light background; crop freely\". I'll place instances and resize to fill card image areas with clipContent.\n\nLet me check one photo component's internal structure to understand how to resize and whether it has auto-layout. Let me inspect Photo_Hero 4:36 and one product photo 4:48, plus an icon 4: