7. Breadcrumb? Not listed explicitly. Build inline per frame.\n28. Color Swatch single? Part of pickers.\n\nThat's ~25+ components. Plus component property setup for swaps. Heavy scripting but let's go step by step, verifying as we go.\n\nAlso I should create these components on a \"components\" area of 03 · Workspace page (e.g., y=-3200..) neatly laid out. The brief says workspace may contain new frames + reusable components. \n\n**Prototype wiring (reactions):**\n- Product Card component → 03_Product (inherited by all instances).\n- Header component cart icon → 04_Cart (inherited).\n- Frame 01: Shop Now button, View All button, Casual tile instance → 02_Category.\n- Frame 02: breadcrumb \"Home\" → 01_Home. Product cards inherit from component ✓.\n- Frame 03: Add to Cart → 04_Cart; breadcrumb \"Shop\" → 02_Category; \"You might also like\" cards inherit ✓.\n- Frame 04: breadcrumb \"Home\" → 01_Home; cart items inherit? Cart Line Item component → 03_Product? Brief 04: \"item → 03_Product\". Set reaction on Cart Line Item component → 03_Product. All 3 items inherit ✓.\n- Header on all frames: cart inherited ✓.\n\nFlow starting points: try setting `prototypeStartNode`... I'll experiment: check if setting works: `frame.prototypeStartNode = true`? Hmm — actually now I really do recall the property: **`prototypeStartNode`** does NOT exist; the correct one might be `frame.flowStartingPoint`? Hmm. Honestly I'll try several in try/catch.\n\nHmm, wait — I now remember the actual plugin API additions (2023): `prototypeStartNode` was added? There's `PageNode.flowStartingPoints: readonly FlowStartingPoint[]` (read-only). And to modify, you... hmm. There's also `figma.notifications`... no.\n\nI'll test: try `f['prototypeStartNode'] = true` in try/catch, then read `page.flowStartingPoints` to see if it registered. If not, try `f['flowStartingPoint']`? hmm, or maybe `figma.root`... Another approach: `page.flowStartingPoints` might be settable? Docs say readonly. There might be no 