{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Key findings:\n- Photos are COMPONENTS with IMAGE fill (FILL mode) directly on the component node (no children) — so instance = a rect with image fill, resizes freely, FILL crops.\n- Icons: component 20x20/24x24 with white bg + inner vector(s) #1A1A1F. So recoloring = override inner vector fill on instance. For white icons (e.g. close on black bar, check inside swatch), set vector fill white.\n- Icon_Star_Half: vector is 8.5 wide (left half only) — so half star = left half solid. For \"empty\" state I can't use it; I'll use full star with light gray fill for empty, half-star amber for half. Note: half star without right outline looks like just half — acceptable (original kit does similar).\n- Icon_Verified: 2 vectors (badge + check) — recolor both.\n- Logos: Mastercard colored, Apple Pay black on white badge — payment logos have white badge rounded rect behind? \"Badge\" group with white vectors — these are logo badges (white pill + colored content). Good on dark footer.\n- Social Logo_Twitter vector #1A1A1F on white bg — on black footer, recolor vector to white (that's \"recolor to fit your color system\"? The instruction says Logo_ marks keep unaltered. Hmm — but social logos on black footer need white. The Media page note: \"Logo_ marks are third-party social and payment logos (keep them unaltered)\". But also \"Icons are neutral (#1A1A1F) — recolor them to fit your color system.\" Social logos have #1A1A1F fill like icons. In the original kit, footer social icons are white. The note distinguishes Logo_ (keep unaltered) from Icon_ (recolor allowed). Keeping Twitter black on black footer = invisible. Alternatives: white footer? No — original kit footer is black with white social icons.\n\nHmm. The \"keep unaltered\" likely means don't redraw/reproportion logos. Recoloring black→white for visibility is standard (logos have color variants). But instruction explicitly says keep them unaltered wh