r vector. For icons on white bg, white square invisible — but set transparent anyway for cleanliness. Wait — the component has white bg + dark vector; if instance fills transparent, glyph remains. Good approach for all icon instances: fills=[], vector recolored as needed.\n\nStar approach with this structure:\n- Star full: instance Icon_Star, fills=[], vector→#FFC633 (amber).\n- Star empty: instance Icon_Star, fills=[], vector→#E4E4E4? Let me pick #DBDBDB... use #E0E0E0.\n- Star half: instance Icon_Star_Half, fills=[], vector→#FFC633. Right half will be empty (transparent). On white bg fine. Hmm — visually a 4.5 rating: 4 full amber + 1 half amber. The half star's missing right half might look odd next to full stars; original kit does exactly this (half star solid left half only). OK.\n\nMy star components: Star/Full, Star/Half, Star/Empty — each a 18x18 frame? Component must be sized: instance of Icon_Star resized to 18x18 (vector scales via SCALE constraints — vector cons=SCALE/SCALE so it scales with component resize ✓).\n\nRating components: frame gap 4, 5 stars 18px → width 5*18+4*4=106, h 18. Variants: 5.0 (5 full), 4.5 (4 full+half), 4.0, 3.5, 3.0. Build via helper.\n\nComponent properties for swap: on Product Card component: addComponentProperty('Photo','INSTANCE_SWAP', 'I4:48')? Default value = component ID of default photo (\"4:48\"). addComponentProperty(name, type, defaultValue) → returns \"Name#id\" key. Then instance.setProperties({'Photo#id': '4:33'}) etc. And 'Rating' INSTANCE_SWAP default Rating/4.5 component id.\n\nWait — do INSTANCE_SWAP property values expect component IDs? Yes, value = component node ID (or name matching). I'll use component IDs.\n\nProduct Card structure (auto-layout vertical, w fixed 295, gap 12, no padding):\n- ImageWrap: frame 295x300 fixed, fill #F0F0F0, r 20, layout HORIZONTAL center/center, clip true. Child: photo instance default 4:48 resized 187x280. Constraints of child inside auto-layout: none needed. When swapping ph