{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>mcp__figma__get_metadata, mcp__figma__use_figma, mcp__figma__whoami</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   Complete a Figma product design benchmark. Assigned file: https://www.figma.com/design/v7DhK3JEKoEZ85CKjv3t3x/ (fileKey `v7DhK3JEKoEZ85CKjv3t3x`). User's request (in Chinese): 在该 Figma 文件中完成完整设计 —— 先读「00·Start Here」的设计任务，参考「01·Foundations」视觉规范，复用「02·Components」组件，使用「04·Media」素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。\n   \n   Benchmark rules (from system): Confirm account is zhengyaozhi@tetras.ai (DONE via whoami). Preserve all reference pages (00/01/02/04) and their nodes. Build everything inside 03 · Workspace (page 6:2, currently empty) — new frames, reusable components, and prototype connections allowed. Use only this file; do not switch accounts/teams. Read-only use_figma for inspection, use_figma for building, get_screenshot to verify all screens, fix and re-verify. Load fonts before text edits. Use valid Plugin API calls. Never use `setPluginData`, `loadAllPagesAsync`, `createImageAsync`. Every assistant message with tool calls MUST start with a line \"Reasoning summary: ...\" ; final response must start with \"Reasoning summary:\" line then \"Final answer:\" and include: assigned file URL, 03·Workspace page ID, screen IDs, prototype work completed, remaining limitations. Unattended session — resolve choices per brief, don't wait for human.\n\n   The design task itself (SHOP.CO fashion e-commerce, L2): Build exactly 4 frames named exactly `01_Home`, `02_Category`, `03_Product`, `04_Cart` (desktop web, 1440 wide, light mode, each scrolls vertically), wire them as a clickable prototype. Brand color #000000 fixed; typefaces fixed: Archivo Black (wordmark + display headings) and Plus Jakarta Sans (all other UI). All other colors, type scale, spacing, radii, elevation, grid are mine to define consistently. Data/copy must match \"Fixed data\" verbatim. Frame names fixed. Evaluation: 1. Checklist coverage per frame 2. Data & copy accuracy 3. Flow & prototype completeness 4. Information hierarchy 5. Visual quality & consistency 6. Component reuse 7. State design.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Figma Plugin API via mcp__figma__use_figma (JS code, 50k char limit per call, `figma.getNodeByIdAsync` NOT `getNodeAsync`)\n   - Component creation: `figma.createComponent()`, `comp.createInstance()`, auto-layout (layoutMode/itemSpacing/padding/primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO vs FIXED/counterAxisAlignItems/layoutGrow for spacers)\n   - Instance overrides allowed: text characters, fills, visibility, size; NOT add/remove children\n   - INSTANCE_SWAP component properties: `comp.addComponentProperty('Photo','INSTANCE_SWAP', defaultComponentId)` → returns key like 'Photo#id'; set per instance via `inst.setProperties({key: componentId})`\n   - Icon tinting pattern: icon components have white node fill + inner VECTOR(s) #1A1A1F → on instance set `inst.fills = []` then walk descendant VECTOR nodes setting fills to target color\n   - Photo components (4:xx) = node-level IMAGE fill with scaleMode FILL → instances resize freely with crop\n   - Reactions (prototype links): `node.reactions = [{ trigger: { type: 'CLICK' }, action: { type: 'NODE', destinationId: '<frameId>', navigation: 'NAVIGATE' } }]` — writable; set on COMPONENT nodes so ALL instances inherit (planned for ProductCard→03_Product, Header cart icon→04_Cart, CartItem→03_Product)\n   - Flow starting points: untested — plan to try `frame.prototypeStartNode = true` (or similar) and verify via `page.flowStartingPoints` readback\n   - Font loading required before any text work: Archivo Black/Regular, Plus Jakarta Sans Regular/Medium/SemiBold/Bold, Inter Regular (createText default)\n   - Strikethrough: `t.textDecoration = 'STRIKETHROUGH'`; underline 'UNDERLINE'\n   - Staging components at negative y on workspace page; frames at y=0 row: 01_Home (0,0), 02_Category (1640,0), 03_Product (3280,0), 04_Cart (4920,0)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Figma file v7DhK3JEKoEZ85CKjv3t3x pages**: 0:1 (00·Start Here, brief frame 5:2), 1:2 (01·Foundations), 1:3 (02·Components), 1:4 (04·Media), 6:2 (03·Workspace — TARGET, was empty)\n   - **Given components**: Button 1:23 (210×52, #000000, r62, PJS Medium 16 white, centered); Text Field 1:26 (400×76, vertical gap10; Label PJS Medium 14 black; Input 400×48 #F0F0F0 r62 padL/R20 cross-CENTER; Placeholder PJS Regular 16 #8C8C8C)\n   - **Media component IDs** (all COMPONENTS, instance them, never move originals):\n     - Photos: Photo_Hero 4:36, Photo_Style_Casual 4:44, Photo_Style_Formal 4:45, Photo_Style_Gym 4:46, Photo_Style_Party 4:47, Photo_Black_Striped_TShirt 4:32, Photo_Checkered_Shirt 4:33, Photo_Courage_Graphic_TShirt 4:49, Photo_Faded_Skinny_Jeans 4:34, Photo_Gradient_Graphic_TShirt 4:35, Photo_Loose_Fit_Bermuda_Shorts 4:37, Photo_Polo_Contrast_Trims 4:40, Photo_Polo_Tipping_Details 4:41, Photo_Skinny_Fit_Jeans 4:42, Photo_Sleeve_Striped_TShirt 4:43, Photo_TShirt_Tape_Details 4:48, Photo_Vertical_Striped_Shirt 4:51, Photo_One_Life_TShirt_1 4:38, _2 4:39, _3 4:50 (product photos 147×220; style photos native: casual 293×220, formal 330×220, gym 147×220, party 275×220; hero 147×220)\n     - Social: Logo_Facebook 4:24, Logo_GitHub 4:25, Logo_Instagram 4:27, Logo_Twitter 4:30\n     - Payment: Logo_Apple_Pay 4:22, Logo_Google_Pay 4:26, Logo_Mastercard 4:28, Logo_PayPal 4:29, Logo_Visa 4:31 (65×48.4 white badge, keep unaltered, resize ~42×31 for footer)\n     - Icons: Icon_Account 4:5, Icon_Arrow_Left 4:4, Icon_Arrow_Right 4:6, Icon_Cart 4:7, Icon_Check 4:8, Icon_Chevron_Down 4:9, Icon_Chevron_Right 4:10, Icon_Close 4:11, Icon_Filter 4:12, Icon_Minus 4:13, Icon_Plus 4:14, Icon_More 4:15, Icon_Search 4:16, Icon_Sparkle 4:17 (56×56), Icon_Star 4:18, Icon_Star_Half 4:19, Icon_Tag 4:20, Icon_Trash 4:21, Icon_Verified 4:23\n   - **Created base components (S1, all on page 6:2 staging area y<0)**: Star/Full 9:2, Star/Half 9:5, Star/Empty 9:8 (18×18); Rating/5.0 9:11, Rating/4.5 9:27, Rating/4.0 9:43, Rating/3.5 9:59, Rating/3.0 9:75 (H-layout gap4, stars-only, patterns: 5.0=FFFFF, 4.5=FFFFH, 4.0=FFFFE, 3.5=FFFHE, 3.0=FFFEE); Field/Search 9:91 (350×48 r62 #F0F0F0, Icon_Search 24 black + \"Search for products...\" PJS Regular 16 #8C8C8C); Stepper/Default 9:96 (H gap16 pad 20/12, #F0F0F0 r62, Minus 20 + \"1\" PJS SemiBold 16 + Plus 20); Button/Outline 9:102 (white bg, #000 stroke 1, r62, pad 28/16, PJS Medium 16 \"Button\"); Button/Checkout 9:104 (352×52 black r62, \"Go to Checkout\" PJS Medium 16 white + Icon_Arrow_Right 24 white). Label text \"COMPONENTS\" at (100,-5480).\n   - **Reusable helper code pattern (re-declare each script)**:\n```js\nfor (const f of [['Archivo Black','Regular'],['Plus Jakarta Sans','Regular'],['Plus Jakarta Sans','Medium'],['Plus Jakarta Sans','SemiBold'],['Plus Jakarta Sans','Bold'],['Inter','Regular']]) {\n  await figma.loadFontAsync({family: f[0], style: f[1]});\n}\nconst ws = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('6:2');\nconst hex = h => ({ r: parseInt(h.slice(1,3),16)/255, g: parseInt(h.slice(3,5),16)/255, b: parseInt(h.slice(5,7),16)/255 });\nconst S = (h, o) => ({ type: 'SOLID', color: hex(h), opacity: o === undefined ? 1 : o });\n// txt(str, pjsStyle, size, hex, {lh, ls, dec}); atxt(str, size, hex) for Archivo Black\n// iconInst(compId, size, tintHex): instance, resize, fills=[], walk children set fills=[S(tintHex)] on vectors\n// place(node): appends to ws at cursor (start cx=100, cy≈-5200 for next script), cx += w+100, wrap x>6600\nconst ICON = { Star:'4:18', StarHalf:'4:19', Verified:'4:23', Close:'4:11', ChevronDown:'4:9', ChevronRight:'4:10', Search:'4:16', Cart:'4:7', Account:'4:5', Filter:'4:12', Minus:'4:13', Plus:'4:14', More:'4:15', ArrowLeft:'4:4', ArrowRight:'4:6', Check:'4:8', Tag:'4:20', Trash:'4:21', Sparkle:'4:17' };\n```\n\n   - **Design system decided**: ink #000000, body gray #616161, muted #8C8C8C, surface #F0F0F0, border #E0E0E0, star amber #FFC633, discount red #FF3333 (solid pill, white text), verified blue #3B82F6. Grid: 1440 frame, 100px side margins → 1240 content. Radii: pills 62, cards/tiles 20. Type: section headings centered Archivo Black 32 uppercase; hero 48/56; wordmark Archivo Black 20; product title Archivo Black 28; \"Order Summary\"/\"All Reviews\" Archivo Black 20; newsletter title Archivo Black 24; brand strip Archivo Black 28; body 16, small 14, tiny 12; prices PJS Bold 20; names PJS SemiBold 16.\n   - **Home page order**: announce → header → hero → brand strip → NEW ARRIVALS (4 cards + View All) → TOP SELLING (4 cards + View All) → BROWSE BY DRESS STYLE (4 tiles, brief order Casual 293/Formal 330/Party 275/Gym 147, gaps 65) → OUR HAPPY CUSTOMERS (3 cards + arrow icons in heading row) → newsletter → footer.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **get_metadata sessionId error**: passed sessionId \"00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000\" → \"Invalid sessionId. Retry without sessionId\" → fixed by omitting sessionId param entirely.\n   - **figma.getNodeAsync not available**: \"no such property 'getNodeAsync' on the figma global object\" → fixed by using `figma.getNodeByIdAsync(id)` instead.\n   - **get_design_context tool not in toolset**: system reminders said to call get_design_context but it isn't among available functions → substituted with read-only use_figma inspection scripts (dumping node trees/fills/fonts), which satisfied the intent.\n   - Note: an unused helper `starComp` (with flawed createComponentFromNode usage) remains defined-but-never-called in S1; actual creation used `starComp2` with `figma.createComponent()` — harmless.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved rating variation inside a single ProductCard component (instances can't add/remove/swap children): built 5 Rating components (stars-only) + plan INSTANCE_SWAP component property 'Rating' on ProductCard so each card instance swaps to correct star pattern; score text (\"4.5/5\") is a separate overridable TEXT node in the card.\n   - Solved photo variation: INSTANCE_SWAP property 'Photo' on ProductCard / StyleTile / CartLineItem; after swap, explicitly resize the photo instance (swap may reset size).\n   - Discount/no-discount cards: component includes old-price + discount pill; per-instance set `visibility=false` when absent.\n   - Icons on dark/colored surfaces: instance fills=[] + tint vectors (white close on black bar, white check inside swatches, amber stars, blue verified, red trash, white arrow/checkout icon).\n   - Style tiles keep native photo aspect (293/330/275/147 ×220) so no distortion; plan STRETCH constraints + ABSOLUTE label overlay.\n   - Prototype at component level: reactions on ProductCard component (→03_Product), Header cart icon (→04_Cart), CartItem component (→03_Product) so all instances inherit; frame-specific links set on instance nodes.\n   - Social logos on black footer: glyphs are white-fill + dark-vector → set instance fills=[] and tint vector white. Payment logos keep white badges as-is.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - “请在以下Figma文件中完成完整设计：Figma 文件：https://www.figma.com/design/v7DhK3JEKoEZ85CKjv3t3x/ 请先阅读「00·Start Here」中的设计任务，参考「01· Foundations」中的视觉规范，复用「02·Components」中的组件，使用「04·Media」中的素材，最终将完整设计交付至「03·Workspace」。”\n   (No other user messages; the rest is benchmark system instruction context.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **S2**: Build components: Announcement Bar (1440×40 black; text PJS Regular 14 white \"Sign up and get 20% off to your first order.\" + \"Sign Up Now\" PJS Medium 14 white underline; Icon_Close 20 white absolute right 24), Header (1440, pad L/R100, wordmark SHOP.CO Archivo Black 20; nav PJS Medium 16 gap32: Shop+ChevronDown/On Sale/New Arrivals/ Brands; spacer layoutGrow; SearchField 9:91 instance; Icon_Cart 24 black with component-level reaction →04_Cart; Icon_Account 24), Newsletter (1240×~176 black r20 pad48, title \"STAY UP TO DATE ABOUT OUR LATEST OFFERS\" Archivo Black 24 white; row: Text Field 1:26 instance label-hidden input-white \"Enter your email address\" + Button 1:23 instance \"Subscribe to Newsletter\"), Footer (1440 black r40 top corners pad 100/64: SHOP.CO Archivo Black 24 + blurb \"We have clothes that suit your style and which you're proud to wear. From women to men.\" + 4 white social glyphs; columns COMPANY: About/Features/Works/Career, HELP: Customer Support/Delivery Details/Terms & Conditions/Privacy Policy, FAQ: Account/Manage Deliveries/Orders/Payments, RESOURCES: Free eBooks/Development Tutorial/How to - Blog/Youtube Playlist; divider; \"Shop.co © 2000-2023, All Rights Reserved\" + 5 payment logos ~42×31)\n   - **S3**: Product Card (295w: ImageWrap 295×300 #F0F0F0 r20 w/ photo 187×280 + Name PJS SemiBold 16 + Rating swap prop + Score text + Price row $price PJS Bold 20 / old PJS Regular 14 #8C8C8C strikethrough / discount pill #FF3333; component-level reaction →03_Product; props 'Photo' & 'Rating' INSTANCE_SWAP, defaults 4:48 & 9:27), Style Tile (293×220 r20, photo STRETCH+ABSOLUTE fill, label overlay PJS SemiBold 20, prop 'Photo'), Review Card (400w white r20 border #E0E0E0 pad28: Rating/5.0 + name PJS SemiBold 18?/16 + Icon_Verified 24 blue + quote PJS Regular 16 #616161), Product Review Card (612w #F0F0F0 r20 pad28: name+verified+More row space-between, Rating swap, quote 14, date 12 #8C8C8C), Cart Line Item (792w #F0F0F0 r20 pad24: photo 100×100 r12 + name/size/color + price/Stepper white-bg override/Trash #FF3333; reaction →03_Product; prop 'Photo')\n   - **S4**: Filter Panel (296: Filters+Icon_Filter; T-shirts/Shorts/Shirts/Hoodie/Jeans rows w/ ChevronRight; Price slider $50–$200; 10 color swatches green #00C12B, red #F50606, yellow #F5DD06, orange #F57906, cyan #06CAF5, blue #063AF5 SELECTED w/ Check, purple #7D06F5, pink #F506A4, white, black; 9 size chips w/ Large selected black; Dress Style rows Casual(current)/Formal/Party/Gym; Apply Filter Button instance), Sort Select, Pagination (Previous/1/2/3/…/8/9/10/Next, current 1 black circle), Gallery (thumbs 3×152² + main 444×530, first selected w/ stroke), Color Picker (olive #4F4631 selected+check, teal #314F4A, navy #31344F), Size Picker (Small/Medium/Large selected/X-Large), Tabs (Product Details/Rating & Reviews CURRENT underline/FAQs + divider), Reviews Toolbar (\"All Reviews\" Archivo 20 + \"(451)\", filter chip, \"Latest\" sort chip, Write a Review Button), Order Summary (416: title Archivo Black 20; Subtotal $565 / Discount (-20%) -$113 red / Delivery Fee $15 / divider / Total $467; promo field white pill Icon_Tag \"Add promo code\" + Apply mini black pill; Button/Checkout 9:104), Hero (1240×640 #F0F0F0 r40: title 48, copy, Shop Now Button, stats 200+/2,000+/30,000+ Archivo 32 w/ dividers, Photo_Hero ~374×560 bottom-bleed, 2 Icon_Sparkle), Brand Strip (NORDE·ATELIER K·MONVALE·RIVA·CASSEL Archivo Black 28 space-between)\n   - **S5–S8**: Assemble 4 frames at (0,0)/(1640,0)/(3280,0)/(4920,0) with instances + per-frame state overrides (header Shop-current on 02/03: Shop black+underline, others #616161; breadcrumb Home›Casual / Home›Shop›Men›T-shirts / Home›Cart)\n   - **S9**: Prototype reactions (component-level + per-frame: 01 Shop Now/View All/Casual tile→02_Category; 02 breadcrumb Home→01_Home; 03 Add to Cart→04_Cart, breadcrumb Shop→02_Category; 04 breadcrumb Home→01_Home; inherited: ProductCard→03, Header cart→04, CartItem→03); test flow starting points (try `frame.prototypeStartNode=true`, verify via `page.flowStartingPoints`)\n   - **S10**: get_screenshot every frame, fix visible problems, re-verify; final answer with file URL, page ID 6:2, frame IDs, prototype summary, limitations\n\n   **Fixed copy to use verbatim**:\n   - Hero: \"FIND CLOTHES THAT MATCH YOUR STYLE\" / \"Browse through our diverse range of meticulously crafted garments, designed to bring out your individuality and cater to your sense of style.\" / \"Shop Now\" / stats: 200+ International Brands · 2,000+ High-Quality Products · 30,000+ Happy Customers\n   - New Arrivals: T-shirt with Tape Details 4.5/5 $120 (4:48); Skinny Fit Jeans 3.5/5 $240 old $260 -20% (4:42); Checkered Shirt 4.5/5 $180 (4:33); Sleeve Striped T-shirt 4.5/5 $130 old $160 -30% (4:43)\n   - Top Selling: Vertical Striped Shirt 5.0/5 $212 old $232 -20% (4:51); Courage Graphic T-shirt 4.0/5 $145 (4:49); Loose Fit Bermuda Shorts 3.0/5 $80 (4:37); Faded Skinny Jeans 4.5/5 $210 (4:34)\n   - Happy Customers (all 5 stars verified): Sarah M. — \"I'm blown away by the quality and style of the clothes I received from Shop.co. From casual wear to elegant dresses, every piece I've bought has exceeded my expectations.\" Alex K. — \"Finding clothes that align with my personal style used to be a challenge until I discovered Shop.co. The range of options they offer is truly remarkable, catering to a variety of tastes and occasions.\" James L. — \"As someone who's always on the lookout for unique fashion pieces, I'm thrilled to have stumbled upon Shop.co. The selection of clothes is not only diverse but also on-point with the latest trends.\"\n   - 02 products: Gradient Graphic T-shirt 3.5/5 $145 (4:35); Polo with Tipping Details 4.5/5 $180 (4:41); Black Striped T-shirt 5.0/5 $120 old $150 -30% (4:32); Skinny Fit Jeans 3.5/5 $240 old $260 -20%; Checkered Shirt 4.5/5 $180; Sleeve Striped T-shirt 4.5/5 $130 old $160 -30%; Vertical Striped Shirt 5.0/5 $212 old $232 -20%; Courage Graphic T-shirt 4.0/5 $145; Loose Fit Bermuda Shorts 3.0/5 $80. Results header: \"Casual\" · \"Showing 1-9 of 100 Products\" · \"Sort by: Most Popular\". Breadcrumb Home › Casual.\n   - 03: \"ONE LIFE GRAPHIC T-SHIRT\" · 4.5/5 · $260 old $300 -13% · \"This graphic t-shirt is perfect for any occasion. Crafted from a soft and breathable fabric, it offers superior comfort and style.\" · Colors olive #4F4631 (selected)/teal #314F4A/navy #31344F · Sizes Small/Medium/Large (selected)/X-Large · qty 1. Tabs: Product Details/Rating & Reviews (current)/FAQs. \"All Reviews (451)\", \"Latest\", \"Write a Review\", \"Load More Reviews\". Reviews: Samantha D. 4.5 \"I absolutely love this t-shirt! The design is unique and the fabric feels so comfortable. As a fellow designer, I appreciate the attention to detail. It's become my favorite go-to shirt.\" Aug 14, 2023; Alex M. 4 \"The t-shirt exceeded my expectations! The colors are vibrant and the print quality is top-notch. Being a UI/UX designer myself, I'm quite picky about aesthetics, and this t-shirt definitely gets a thumbs up from me.\" Aug 15, 2023; Ethan R. 3.5 \"This t-shirt is a must-have for anyone who appreciates good design. The minimalistic yet stylish pattern caught my eye, and the fit is perfect. I can see the designer's touch in every aspect of this shirt.\" Aug 16, 2023; Olivia P. 4 \"As a UI/UX enthusiast, I value simplicity and functionality. This t-shirt not only represents those principles but also feels great to wear. It's evident that the designer poured their creativity into making this t-shirt stand out.\" Aug 17, 2023; Liam K. 4 \"This t-shirt is a fusion of comfort and creativity. The fabric is soft, and the design speaks volumes about the designer's skill. It's like wearing a piece of art that reflects my passion for both design and fashion.\" Aug 18, 2023; Ava H. 4.5 \"I'm not just wearing a t-shirt; I'm wearing a piece of design philosophy. The intricate details and thoughtful layout of the design make this shirt a conversation starter.\" Aug 19, 2023. You might also like: Polo with Contrast Trims 4.0/5 $212 old $242 -20% (4:40); Gradient Graphic T-shirt 3.5/5 $145; Polo with Tipping Details 4.5/5 $180; Black Striped T-shirt 5.0/5 $120 old $150 -30%. Breadcrumb Home › Shop › Men › T-shirts.\n   - 04: \"YOUR CART\"; items: Gradient Graphic T-shirt Size: Large Color: White $145 qty 1 (4:35); Checkered Shirt Size: Medium Color: Red $180 qty 1 (4:33); Skinny Fit