{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"S2 done. Global components:\n- Announcement Bar 10:2\n- Header 10:7\n- Newsletter 10:37\n- Footer 10:46\n\nText field hidden label worked (h=48). Now S3: Product Card, Style Tile, Review Card, Product Review Card, Cart Line Item.\n\nProductCard (295 wide):\n- Vertical auto-layout, hug height, gap 12\n- ImageWrap: 295×300, #F0F0F0, r20, layout HORIZONTAL center+center; photo instance 187×280 (component photo 4:48 default \"TShirt Tape Details\")\n- Name: \"T-shirt with Tape Details\" PJS SemiBold 16 #000000\n- RatingRow: H gap 4 center: rating instance (component 9:27 Rating/4.5 default) + score text \"4.5/5\" PJS SemiBold 14? — spec: score \"4.5/5\" — PJS SemiBold 14 #000000. Layout: stars then score.\n- PriceRow: H gap 8 center: price \"$120\" PJS Bold 20; old price \"$260\" PJS Regular 14 #8C8C8C strikethrough; discount pill: frame 36×22? auto pill #FF3333 r62, pad 8/6? text \"-20%\" PJS Medium 12 white. pill padding L/R 8, T/B 5 → hug.\n- INSTANCE_SWAP props: 'Photo' default component 4:48; 'Rating' default 9:27. Also boolean props? For oldPrice visibility and discount visibility: componentProp BOOLEAN 'showOld' and 'showDiscount' — set visible on component nodes then addComponentProperty. Simpler: addComponentProperty('showOld','BOOLEAN',true) — binds to oldPrice text visible. Similarly 'showDiscount' bound to pill. Then per-instance setProperties({['showOld#key']:false}).\n\nWait, addComponentProperty requires the propertyName referenced nodes: component.addComponentProperty(name, type, defaultValue) then it returns the key; but binding to node: need node.componentPropertyReferences = { visible: key }. For INSTANCE_SWAP: componentPropertyReferences = { mainComponent: key }? Hmm: for instance swap, you set property on the component whose property references the INSTANCE node inside the component. Actually INSTANCE_SWAP property is attached to a child instance node: childInstance.componentPropertyReferences = { mainComponent: propertyName }? Let me recall Plugin API: `componentPropertyReferences` on a node: for TEXT: { characters }; for BOOLEAN: { visible }; for INSTANCE_SWAP: { mainComponent }; for SWAP: { ... }. And addComponentProperty(component, name, type, defaultValue). The returned key is like 'Photo#12:34'.\n\nSo:\n- photoInst = imageWrap child instance; key = comp.addComponentProperty('Photo','INSTANCE_SWAP','4:48')? defaultValue must be component id string. Then photoInst.componentPropertyReferences = { mainComponent: key }? Hmm wait — actually I recall the property must be added first, then set on the instance node. Let me just do that; if error, adjust.\n- ratingInst similar with 'Rating', default '9:27'.\n- nameText: 'Name' TEXT property: key = comp.addComponentProperty('Name','TEXT','T-shirt with Tape Details'); nameText.componentPropertyReferences={characters:key}.\n- priceText: 'Price' TEXT, '$120'. oldText: 'OldPrice' TEXT '$260'. scoreText: 'Score' TEXT '4.5/5'. discountText 'Discount' TEXT '-20%'.\n- boolean: 'ShowOld' BOOLEAN true bound to oldText visible; 'ShowDiscount' BOOLEAN true bound to pill visible.\n\nThat gives clean instance overrides via setProperties: {['Name#..']: '...', ...} using returned keys stored per component. Since I'll create 9+ instances later across frames with different values, I need the key strings. I'll store in returned JSON.\n\nText auto-resize: name width 295 fixed → textAutoResize 'HEIGHT', resize(295, h). Price row hug.\n\nStyleTile (293×220 r20):\n- frame 293×220, fill #F0F0F0? photo covers all → fill irrelevant but keep.\n- photo instance fill entire: 293×220, scaleMode FILL handles crop. constraints STRETCH.\n- label overlay: absolute bottom-left 24,20: \"Casual\" PJS SemiBold 20 #000000 (on light photos, black text per original SHOP.CO design — yes original uses black text on light tiles).\n- INSTANCE_SWAP 'Photo' default 4:44 (Casual). Store key.\n- Component name 'Style Tile'. For Formal (330×220), Party (275×220), Gym (147×220) instances: resize instance after creation; photo instance inside with STRETCH constraints will follow.\n\nReviewCard (400 wide) for Home testimonials:\n- V layout pad 28, gap 12, white fill, r20, stroke #E0E0E0\n- Row: rating instance (Rating/5.0) + verified row (name + verified icon) — original layout: stars top, then name + verified check on same row, then quote.\n  Row1: rating 9:11 instance.\n  Row2: H gap 8 center: name \"Sarah M.\" PJS SemiBold 18? use 16; Icon_Verified 24 blue tint.\n  Quote: PJS Regular 16 #616161 lh 24, width 344 fixed (400-56), autoResize HEIGHT.\n- TEXT prop 'Name', 'Quote' maybe — instances only on home; simpler to override characters directly on instance children? Overriding instance child text characters is allowed. But cleaner with component props. Only 3 instances with unique text; direct child override is fine. I'll do direct overrides later (find by name). Keep names: 'name', 'quote'.\n\nProductReviewCard (612 wide) for 03:\n- #F0F0F0 r20 pad 28, V gap 12\n- Row1 H space-between center (width 612-56=556 fixed): left H gap 8 center: name PJS SemiBold 16 + verified 24 blue; right Icon_More 24 #000000? black dots.\n- Row2: rating instance (default Rating/4.5) — swap prop? Reviews have 4.5/4.0/3.5/4.0/4.0/4.5. Add INSTANCE_SWAP 'Rating' default 9:27.\n- Quote PJS Regular 14 #616161 lh 22 width 556.\n- Date PJS Regular 12 #8C8C8C.\n\nCartLineItem (792 wide):\n- #F0F0F0 r20, pad 24, H gap 16, height 124? content: photo 100×100 r12; middle V gap 4: name PJS SemiBold 16? Actually original cart: name bold 16? name 16 semi; \"Size: Large\" 14 #616161; \"Color: White\" 14; right side V? Original layout: photo left; center col name/size/color; right col: price top-right, stepper below price, trash icon bottom-right. Let me structure: H: photo; spacer; colMid (V gap 4): name, size, color; spacer grow; colRight (V, alignItems END, gap 8): price PJS Bold 16? \"$145\" bold; stepper instance (white bg override); trash icon 20 red.\n- Stepper instance white: set fills=[S('#FFFFFF')].\n- Trash: Icon_Trash 20 tint #FF3333.\n- INSTANCE_SWAP 'Photo' default 4:35. Reaction → 03_Product added in S9 (component-level, all instances inherit... wait CartItem click → 03 Product makes sense).\n\nAlso add 'Price' TEXT prop? Only 3 instances; direct override fine.\n\nNames for later lookup: 'photo', 'stepper', 'trash', 'name', 'size', 'color', 'price', 'rating'.\n\nWrite S3 now. Careful: addComponentProperty returns key; wrap in try/catch to report errors per property. If componentPropertyReferences assignment fails, properties won't bind; report.\n\nAlso for photo swap: when instance swaps to different photo component, size may reset to native (147×220 etc). ImageWrap has layout: photo centered, fixed 187×280 regardless. After swap I'll resize photo instance in frame assembly (S5-S8): find child 'photo' and resize(187,280). The wrap is fixed 295×300 with center alignment so photo smaller still fine — but scaleMode FILL crops to the instance's own bounds; different aspect just crops differently. Good.\n\nLet me write the script.","signature":"0dd3df7f3fcc4401b23fed67"}],"id":"a3a25d1e-1fa7-477e-9bb6-3ab1fc8fad32","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e0442a0-e797-4be3-bd46-d253cafd84e1","uuid":"46d460ae-8d1a-43ff-9dd8-970557a38c51","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:07:53.252Z","thinking_duration_ms":42858}
