{"type":"assistant","message":{"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I see:\n- Hero 1240×640 ✓, Brand Strip ✓, Newsletter ✓\n- Sections: 1240×10 height — not hugging! Their children ARE laid out (deeper: heading 272×35, row 1240×399, button 52) but the section frame height stays 10.\n\nWhy? Section frames: layoutMode VERTICAL, primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO, counterAxisSizingMode FIXED, resize(1240,10). Children sum ~35+40+399+40+52+40=606 but height stuck at 10.\n\nAh — I bet the issue: `sec.resize(1240, 10)` called AFTER setting primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'? In my code: \n```\nsec.layoutMode = 'VERTICAL';\nsec.primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO';\nsec.counterAxisSizingMode = 'FIXED';\nsec.resize(1240, 10);\n```\nresize() on an auto-layout frame with primary AUTO: resize sets width AND height explicitly — when you resize a frame with primaryAxisSizingMode AUTO, Figma switches primary sizing to FIXED? Actually `resize` sets width/height; for auto-layout frames the docs say resize() overrides sizing modes — yes! \"resize() will set primaryAxisSizingMode and counterAxisSizingMode to FIXED\" — I recall resize() forces fixed dimensions. That explains height 10 stuck: sections became FIXED height 10 (children overflow).\n\nSame problem in the earlier helper `hcenter` (unused here) and — importantly — the same pattern was used in S2/S3/S4 scripts in several places: e.g., Product Card: comp.resize(295,100) after setting AUTO → became FIXED 295×100? But Product Card instances showed correct height (row 1240×399 implies cards ~399 incl spacing? row height 399 = card height ~399? Actually a card = 300 img + 12 + name + 12 + rating + 12 + price ≈ 380-400). And Newsletter 174 ✓. Header 96 fixed by design ✓. Footer 373 — I explicitly set primary AUTO then resize(1440, comp.height) → resize again forced FIXED 1440×373; fine since 373 was correct at that moment.\n\nBut the sections in 01_Home are broken (height 10). Also review-section/dressstyle same pattern → 10 high.\n\nFix approach: for each broken section frame, set `primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'` again (after resize) — setting the mode back to AUTO re-hugs. Setting property (not resize) does not force fixed. So repair: iterate content children (sections) → primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'.\n\nAlso check: does the same bug affect 'content' frame itself (1440×104)? Yes! content.resize(1440,10) → height fixed 10?? But content shows 104 — resize(1440,10) then children appended → hmm 104 ≠ 10. Because resize happened BEFORE children were appended; after appending children, primaryAxisSizingMode was FIXED so height should stay 10... it shows 104 = padding sum. Odd but whatever: 104 is wrong too; children (Hero 640 + 64 + strip 40 + ...) should make it ~2600. So content also broken.\n\nAnd frame 16:2 itself: resize(1440,200) after AUTO → FIXED 200 height; footer instance 373 overflows outside. Need frame.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'.\n\nRoot cause understood: resize() on auto-layout frames forces both axes FIXED. Repair script: \n- frame 16:2: primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'\n- content: primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'\n- each section frame: primaryAxisSizingMode = 'AUTO'\n\nAlso other places where I used the same anti-pattern earlier:\n- S2 Newsletter: comp.resize(1240,100) after AUTO... then reported height was hug-correct? I later did not resize again; Newsletter shows 174 ✓ (it printed 174 above). Hmm — resize(1240,100) happened at creation before appending children; then children appended → height stayed... but it shows 174. Confusing. Maybe resize() only forces FIXED if the frame is empty?? Or the docs: \"resize() resizes the node... for auto-layout frames, if children overflow they...\" Actually maybe resize() does NOT change sizing modes (I misremembered). Then why are sections stuck at 10?\n\nAlternative explanation: sections were created and resize(1240,10) — AUTO mode recomputes on child add; children were added BEFORE appending sec to content... but wait, deeper shows children properly laid out inside the section (row 399 high). So section's children are laid out but section height stuck 10 despite primary AUTO? That suggests primaryAxisSizingMode is actually FIXED.\n\nLet me just read primaryAxisSizingMode of a section and of content to diagnose, then fix accordingly.","signature":"cca4404332fc47e4866ae6d6"}],"id":"800ba163-7121-41bf-b078-212ca32281b4","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e0442a0-e797-4be3-bd46-d253cafd84e1","uuid":"6cc7e1ae-7999-4881-bd32-9e41045db036","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:16:12.465Z","thinking_duration_ms":24875}
