ng AUTO/AUTO, no resize — fine. main: same, fine. sec: `sec.resize(1240, 10)` AFTER setting AUTO → forced FIXED again! Same bug. row/row2: no resize, fine. also: resize after AUTO → FIXED.\n\nSo the bug hits: 02 content? In 02's script (before compaction) I likely had the same pattern. And 03's content, sec, also; 04's content, main (no resize — fine), items (no resize — fine).\n\nWait, but for 03's content the children ARE appended and would show correct sizes individually, but the container is FIXED at whatever height. Fix: walk the frames 16:3/16:4/16:5 and re-set primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' on all vertical auto-layout frames (and counterAxisSizingMode AUTO for horizontal hug frames where needed). Actually safer: targeted repair — for each frame, set content.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO', and for children that are VERTICAL auto-layout with counterAxis FIXED at 1240, keep counterAxis FIXED (width fixed 1240 is desired). For horizontal rows (main, rows, row2), primary should be AUTO (hug width) — setting primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' is right for them too.\n\nBut careful: sec also has resize(1240,10) → counterAxisSizingMode FIXED 1240 (desired width), primary FIXED → set primary AUTO. also same. main (horizontal, both AUTO, no resize) fine.\n\nAlso inner components: the section containers inside 01_Home were repaired already. What about 02's inner containers (results, etc.)? Earlier read showed results 909×1367 correct — good.\n\nAlso, Announcement/Header/Footer are instances — fine.\n\nAdditionally check the 'also' heading and row2 heights after fix.\n\nPlan: one script: for f in [16:3,16:4,16:5]: content=f.children.find('content'); content.primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO'; then for sec/also in 03: set AUTO; return fresh heights. Actually setting primaryAxisSizingMode on a frame recalculates immediately? Should. Then read heights again in a follow-up.","signature":"3a0f3e3d67c04d04a6dc927b"}],"id":"3ff51707-673d-49f6-863d-62acc4047880","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"a