 Striped T-shirt $120 old $260 -30%\" — hmm, conflicting with $150?\n\nWait no — look again at summary pending list: \"3×3 grid of 9 product cards via makeCard\" — data for category grid wasn't fully spelled out in the summary except in section 3's example: \"corrected filter size chips...\" — the category grid data was in the original brief dump. The summary says for 03 also-like: \"Black Striped T-shirt 5.0 $120 old $150 -30% 4:32\". And category Black Striped might be $120 old $260? Hmm, that'd be odd for the same product to have two old prices, but the brief itself may list different prices per section (it's mock data — indeed home TOP SELLING Vertical Striped $212 $232, category Vertical Striped $212 $260?).\n\nHmm, actually let me check the brief directly rather than guessing. The brief frame is 5:2 on page 0:1. I dumped it fully before compaction. Rather than re-dump everything, search for the product tables. Let me read the brief text and grep the relevant table rows. The brief is large; I'll extract text and filter lines containing '$'.","signature":"3761c29f351d47cda439aca5"}],"id":"3095a642-59b6-4497-b6a9-bfdb09857851","model":"glm-5.3-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7e0442a0-e797-4be3-bd46-d253cafd84e1","uuid":"696fc6f9-a725-4874-879b-17bed093ec94","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:35:11.539Z","thinking_duration_ms":17930}
